/-! # Constructible finite-Tor dévissage with lisse coefficients

Source: latest blueprint, part-duality-trace-formula/sec-lefschetz-verdier/
sec-kunneth-formulas-and-external-duality/sk-thm-sf-kunneth-verdier/
lem-trf-devissage-generation.md and its proof, Steps 0--3;
Wei Yang, Zulip #1441, item 27 (2026-11-02).
(blueprint: lem-trf-devissage-generation).

The generators use the published local finite-presentation predicate and flatness
on native coefficient modules, extended through their scheme-theoretic closures.
Over finite A, finite flat stalks are finite projective, without a self-injectivity
hypothesis. The final statement retains the failure of generation by constants.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale
open scoped CategoryTheory.Obj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

/-- Lisse flat stratum extensions in the native condensed coefficient category.
For finite discrete A, the recorded local finite-presentation condition is local
constancy with finite A-module stalks: a finite presentation matrix of sections of
A becomes a constant matrix after a pro-etale cover. Together with flatness its
local models are finite projective, equivalently summands of finite free modules.
The extension is the existing a_! = g_*j_! through the scheme-theoretic closure.
Source: latest blueprint lem-trf-devissage-generation, displayed generators,
with Wei Yang #1441, item 27 (blueprint: lem-trf-devissage-generation). -/
def trfLisseFlatStratumGenerators
    (T : WeilConjectures.FiniteTraceFormulaConventions.{u})
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian X] : ObjectProperty (T.Complexes X) :=
  fun K ↦ ∃ (U : Scheme.{u}) (a : U ⟶ X) (ha : IsImmersion a)
    (L : Mod (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology U) Ab.{u + 1}) (T.coefficientSheaf U)),
    IsLocallyFinitelyPresented (T.coefficientSheaf U) L ∧ ObjectProperty.flat L ∧
      Nonempty (K ≅ (_root_.DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj
        ((coefficientHeartLocallyClosedExtension T.coefficients a ha).obj L))

/-- The constant-coefficient subclass of the stratum-extension generators.
`Mod.regular` is precisely A_U. The recorded extension is j_! followed by g_*
through the scheme-theoretic image, placed in degree zero. Exactness of closed
pushforward identifies this with Rg_*j_!A_U. All locally closed immersions are
allowed; on Noetherian X each occurs in a finite constructible stratification.
Source: latest blueprint lem-trf-devissage-generation, last sentence and proof Step 3
(blueprint: lem-trf-devissage-generation). -/
def trfConstantStratumGenerators
    (T : WeilConjectures.FiniteTraceFormulaConventions.{u})
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian X] : ObjectProperty (T.Complexes X) :=
  fun K ↦ ∃ (U : Scheme.{u}) (a : U ⟶ X) (ha : IsImmersion a),
    Nonempty (K ≅ (_root_.DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj
      ((coefficientHeartLocallyClosedExtension T.coefficients a ha).obj
        (Mod.regular (T.coefficientSheaf U))))

/-- D^b_ctf(X,A) is the thick subcategory generated by Rg_*j_!L with L lisse flat.
The zero seed makes the intersection-of-thick-subcategories convention explicit,
including empty X. The lisse condition uses the recorded finite-projective local
models, which are equivalent to finite flat stalks for finite A.
Source: latest blueprint lem-trf-devissage-generation and proof Steps 0--2,
with Wei Yang #1441, item 27 (blueprint: lem-trf-devissage-generation).

Proof:
1. X is Noetherian by lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian. Apply
   sk-lem-sf-flat-model to obtain a bounded flat constructible representative P,
   over the given A itself.
2. det-sf-flat-model-generation gives finite ordered strata and a finite filtration
   of each flat term by a_!L. Its local finite flat modules are finitely presented
   because A is finite, hence projective by
   lem-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-flat-module-projective. They are summands of
   finite free modules only after local trivialization; L stays lisse globally.
3. Factor a through its scheme-theoretic closure. The complementary open is
   quasi-compact on Noetherian X. lem-exc-proetale-closed-exact gives Rg_*=g_*.
   lem-weil-pbc-complex-ses-triangle turns each filtration step into a triangle.
4. lem-weil-pbc-bounded-complex-triangulated-devissage applies the finite stupid
   filtration of P, with quotients P^q[-q], to obtain the forward inclusion.
5. Conversely lisse flat generators have Tor amplitude [0,0]; open extension and
   exact closed pushforward preserve constructibility and finite Tor amplitude.
   Clause (3) of det-sf-flat-model-generation gives thickness and generator
   membership. The universal property in pur9-def-thick gives reverse inclusion.
No cohomology truncation of a perfect A-complex is assumed perfect, and no A-input
is restricted to Z/ell^N. -/
theorem trf_constructibleFiniteTor_eq_thick_lisse
    (T : WeilConjectures.FiniteTraceFormulaConventions.{u})
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [X.Over (Spec (.of T.datum.k))]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (X ↘ Spec (.of T.datum.k))]
    [QuasiCompact (X ↘ Spec (.of T.datum.k))]
    [IsSeparated (X ↘ Spec (.of T.datum.k))] :
    T.constructibleFiniteTor X = ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope
      ((fun K ↦ ∃ (hX : IsNoetherian X), @trfLisseFlatStratumGenerators T X hX K) ⊔
        IsZero) := by
  sorry

/-- Constant stratum extensions do not generate in general: the quadratic Kummer
example over Fbar_5 with F_3 coefficients. The ambient category and Dctf are exactly
those of the preceding generation equality. A structure map and its geometric
properties are included to witness the same separated finite-type hypotheses.
Source: latest blueprint lem-trf-devissage-generation, last sentence and proof Step 3
(blueprint: lem-trf-devissage-generation).

Proof: take k_0=F_5, k its algebraic closure, ell=3, A=F_3 and X=G_m.
lem-trf-kummer-monodromy supplies an exact fibre functor F, a natural endomorphism
monodromy-minus-identity t, and a lisse flat sheaf L. Transport these along the
canonical finite-coefficient comparison of the conventions. The endomorphism is
zero on every constant stratum extension and is not nilpotent on L. By
lem-trf-nilpotent-fiber-homology the complexes on whose every cohomology it is
nilpotent form a thick subcategory. pur9-def-thick therefore places the constant
thick closure inside it. L[0] is outside it, and belongs to Dctf by the generator
membership above. This proves the displayed existential obstruction. -/
theorem trf_constants_do_not_generate :
    ∃ T : WeilConjectures.FiniteTraceFormulaConventions.{u},
      T.datum.p = 5 ∧ T.ell = 3 ∧ Nat.card T.A = 3 ∧
      ∃ (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of T.datum.k))
        (hX : IsNoetherian X) (K : T.Complexes X),
        LocallyOfFiniteType f ∧ QuasiCompact f ∧ IsSeparated f ∧
        Nonempty (X ≅ Spec (.of (LaurentPolynomial T.datum.k))) ∧
        T.constructibleFiniteTor X K ∧
        ¬ ObjectProperty.triangEnvelope (@trfConstantStratumGenerators T X hX ⊔ IsZero) K := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale
